  "answer": "Your report is very short, so this match is probable but not certain. Two earlier tickets describe PowerToys 0.100.x where the Settings window won't open. In #48947 (0.100.2), double-clicking the tray icon did nothing and Quick Access showed an error. The reporter fixed it by fully uninstalling PowerToys and reinstalling it, and said it was working afterwards. In #48432, Settings and Quick Access failed with a 'You must install .NET Desktop Runtime' dialog even though .NET was installed. That ticket reports it on all 0.100.x versions, including a manual reinstall of 0.100.2. One commenter there said v0.99.1 did not have the problem. Scoop users fixed it with `scoop update` and then `scoop update powertoys --force`, but that doesn't apply to a GitHub install. Next steps: fully uninstall PowerToys, then reinstall it with the official installer. If Settings still won't open, check whether a .NET Desktop Runtime dialog appears. If it does, you could go back to v0.99.1 until a fix is out. If the problem continues, please file a new ticket with your Windows version, the exact error or behavior, and a Bug Report ZIP file."
